<!--
Rainforest: a monstera leaf, holes and all.

  It replaces a dome on a stem with a line under it, which was a lollipop, and
  was the same drawing as the savannah's tree with the top rounded off.

  The holes are the point. Two attempts cut *notches* into the outline instead,
  and an edge that narrows and widens four times reads as scallops — scalloped
  and stacked is a fir tree, which is what both of them looked like. The plant
  is famous for its fenestrations, and a hole is a shape the eye reads instantly
  with no risk of being mistaken for an edge.

  Big and quiet: it sits at 108dp behind a zone card at 10% of the area's
  accent, which is a size that can carry real drawing. A glyph's worth of detail
  at that scale is what made the old marks look unfinished.

  Drawn in white and tinted at the call site with the zone's own ZoneAccent, so
  one drawable serves whatever colour the floor plan gives an area. The 54%
  paths stay proportionally lighter after tinting — `Icon` multiplies alpha
  rather than replacing it.
-->
